node_modules/

# Not committed, deliberately.
#
# The three components are installed from their default branches, so a lockfile
# would pin the commits and CI would stop being able to catch a change in one
# of them breaking the join — which is the only reason this application's CI
# exists. The cost is that an install is not byte-reproducible; that is the
# right trade for a repository whose job is to prove the four still fit
# together, and the wrong one for anything being deployed.
package-lock.json
